From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:01:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 76/79] runner: no drawn digit right after an owned inline
 integer in reasoning, and a reasoning digit-run cap

On Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TP2 the model kept extending owned inline values (7^64, 7^216, 7^220, 7^222) by
1,600-29,700 invented digits: the runner splices ` <digits>` with nothing after it (TF_RUNNER_INLINE_MARK=0), so
the next draw can continue the number. Every runaway seen (agent-client replies to a 7^222 mod 1000003 task, on
the engine before this commit, with and without a thinking budget) began with the exact engine value; a reply then
hit its 8192 budget cut or max_tokens (finish=length at 32768) before it answered.

The TP2 backend has no masked draws, so the stop works as the call gate and the budget cut do: the runner's new
RunnerHook.stop names a drawn token to replace where a round's tokens land (round_cut.apply, the MTP/windowed
path) and a pipelined step reads a watched draw before feeding it. In reasoning only: the model's first token
after an owned inline value ending in a digit may not start with a digit, and a digit run stops past
TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_RUN_MAX (default 1024; 0 off); the stopped token becomes a newline. TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_STOP=0 turns
the first off. Forced rows are never replaced; fence, REPL and trace results (newline tails) never arm it;
thinking-off replies are unchanged. The newline token is looked up at the first arm or near the cap.

runner.zig stays under 600 lines: its knob helpers moved to runner_knob.zig, its test list to runner_tests.zig.
Tests (test-digit-stop-host): the rules on token text, the fake target's MTP and pipelined rounds and sessions,
each beside a negative control; mutating either lanes call site fails the fake-target tests.
